[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 703,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 466,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107468,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 415,
        "headingId": 466,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Renal Ewing sarcoma, like other extraosseous Ewing sarcomas, is a sarcoma composed of small round cells, characterized by a fusion of a FET gene family member (most frequently <em>EWSR1</em>) and an ETS gene family member (most frequently <em>FLI1</em>).</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:09:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 704,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 467,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107469,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 415,
        "headingId": 467,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>9364/3 Renal Ewing sarcoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:09:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 705,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 468,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107470,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 415,
        "headingId": 468,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2B52.3 Ewing sarcoma of soft tissue</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:09:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 706,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 469,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107471,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 415,
        "headingId": 469,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> peripheral neuroectodermal tumour; Ewing sarcoma family of tumours.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:09:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 707,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 470,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107472,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 415,
        "headingId": 470,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:09:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 708,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 471,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107473,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 415,
        "headingId": 471,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Renal parenchyma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:09:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 709,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 472,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107474,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 415,
        "headingId": 472,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>There are no specific symptoms or imaging characteristics that may distinguish Ewing sarcoma from other primary renal tumours, but a classic triad of haematuria, pain, and palpable tumour has been reported.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:09:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 710,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 473,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107475,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 415,
        "headingId": 473,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Ewing sarcoma is the second most common sarcoma of bone and soft tissues in children and adolescents, representing 2&ndash;3% of cancers in these age groups. Primary Ewing sarcoma of the kidney is extremely rare, representing 1.5% of all cases of Ewing sarcoma in one study. The median patient age is 27&nbsp;years, and there is a slight male preponderance {23761687}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:09:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 711,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 474,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107476,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 415,
        "headingId": 474,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>See <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/chaptercontent/44/206\" target=\"_blank\">section </a><em>Ewing sarcoma</em> .</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:09:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 712,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 475,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107477,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 415,
        "headingId": 475,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>See <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/chaptercontent/44/206\" target=\"_blank\">section </a><em>Ewing sarcoma</em> .</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:09:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 719,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 482,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107478,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 415,
        "headingId": 482,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>There are no specific gross features, but tumours are usually large (110&ndash;120&nbsp;mm on average).</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:09:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 713,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 476,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107479,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 415,
        "headingId": 476,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The morphology of renal Ewing sarcoma is identical to that of Ewing sarcoma in other bone or soft tissue locations. Because most cases occur in adolescents, diagnosis will frequently be biopsy-based. The aspect of a highly cellular tumour composed of small cells with little cytoplasm, organized in sheets and possibly rosettes, should stimulate the use of ancillary techniques. Diffuse strong membranous CD99 expression is a hallmark, although molecular confirmation is recommended {17134738}. In addition, nuclear NKX2-2 staining in &ge;&nbsp;5% of tumour cells shows high sensitivity but imperfect specificity for Ewing sarcoma {22446943}. A panel of markers, including WT1, SMARCB1 (INI1), keratins, neuroendocrine markers, desmin, PAX8, PHOX2B, and NB84, may be used to exclude other entities, such as blastemal Wilms tumour, neuroblastoma, malignant rhabdoid tumour, and desmoplastic round cell tumour. It should be noted that as many as 30% of Ewing sarcomas may show keratin expression, which should not lead to an erroneous diagnosis of undifferentiated carcinoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:09:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 714,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 477,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107480,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 415,
        "headingId": 477,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:09:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 715,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 478,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107481,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 415,
        "headingId": 478,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The majority (90%) of Ewing sarcomas, including renal Ewing sarcoma, show a characteristic t(11;22)(q24;q12) translocation with fusion between various exons of the genes <em>EWSR1</em> and <em>FLI1</em>. In addition, translocations of <em>EWSR1</em> with a number of other ETS genes (including <em>ERG</em>, <em>ETV1</em>, and <em>FEV</em>), or between another gene (<em>FUS</em>) and ETS-family genes, have been described {21872822}. Together, these translocations are found in almost 100% of cases.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:09:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 718,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 481,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107482,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 415,
        "headingId": 481,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> typical (small blue round cell) morphology with diffuse strong membranous CD99 staining.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:09:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 716,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 479,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107483,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 415,
        "headingId": 479,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>No separate staging system exists for renal Ewing sarcoma, but the staging system for renal cell carcinoma from the International Society of Paediatric Oncology (SIOP) 2016 UMBRELLA protocol or from the Children&rsquo;s Oncology Group (COG) may be used.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:09:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 717,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 480,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107484,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 415,
        "headingId": 480,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The current overall survival rate for patients with localized renal Ewing sarcoma is about 70%, but it drops to 10&ndash;40% for those with metastases at diagnosis {23761687}. No other predictive factors are currently known. The presence of vascular thrombus and the exact nature of the molecular genetic translocation do not seem to affect the prognosis.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:09:19"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]